  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the Burmese Roofed Turtle, Batagur trivittata, on the Upper Chindwin River,..Myanmar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the Burmese Roofed Turtle, Batagur trivittata, on the Upper Chindwin River, Myanmar. In partnership with Wildlife Conservation Society, this project will support conservation efforts that will put the Batagur trivittata on a trajectory towards a genetically diverse, self-sustaining wild population. Specific activities include: (1) incubation of trivittata eggs; (2) create modern facilities to host head-starting turtles and a captive assurance population; (3) conduct surveys of the Chindwin River and tributaries in the Htamanthi Wildlife Sanctuary for hitherto over-looked populations; (4) expand nest protection, head-starting, and threat abatement programs to encompass new areas found to be inhabited by B. trivittata; (5) initiate a trial release program of juvenile B. trivittata; (6) increase the safety of those released hatchlings through patrols, education, and incentives for turtle protection.</narrative>
  </description>
